      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "The fog adds light only where a real light reaches the air. It takes nothing from the ambient light (Lighting window \u203A Environment \u203A Environment Lighting). So the air in a shadow stays black, while the surfaces in that shadow still get the ambient.\n\n<b>Predict:</b> The Panel casts a shadow through the lamp's beam. You make the ambient light much brighter. Will the air under the Panel get lighter?\n\n<b>Try:</b>\n1. In the Lighting window, Environment \u203A Environment Lighting, set Ambient Color to a light grey.\n2. Compare the Panel's underside and the floor with the air below the Panel.\n3. Set Ambient Color back to (0.02, 0.025, 0.035).\n\n<size=85%><color=#A8A8A8>Reference: References 10, 11, 12</color></size>"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 2f7116f10747a67409388e93052ae222, type: 2}
