  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "Fog dims what lies behind it and adds the light that reaches it. Where the wall casts a shadow into the fog, no light is added; the lit air between the shadows is a shaft. Fog scatters light mostly forward, in the direction the light travels. Anisotropy sets how strongly.\n\n<b>Predict:</b> A light shines through the slit from behind the wall. Seen looking toward the light, and seen looking away from it, where is the shaft brighter?\n\n<b>Try:</b>\n1. Look through both cameras of this station.\n2. On the light's Volumetric Additional Light component, set Anisotropy to 0, then back to 0.7.\n3. Walk the Scene view camera around the shaft.\n\n<size=85%><color=#A8A8A8>Reference: References 05\u201311 \xB7 Liminal Kit, B \xB7 Slit wall</color></size>"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 2f7116f10747a67409388e93052ae222, type: 2}
